<% page_title @course.title %>
<% page_description @course.summary %>
<% content_for :wide, true %>
<% sample = @course.sample_post %>

<div class="page-grid">
  <p class="eyebrow">A course by <%= Profile.full_name %></p>
  <h1><%= @course.title %></h1>
  <p class="lede"><%= @course.summary %></p>

  <aside class="rail">
    <dl class="facts">
      <%# The price shows once there is somewhere to buy it. %>
      <% if @course.on_sale? %>
        <dt>price</dt>
        <dd class="course-price"><strong><%= number_to_currency(@course.price, precision: 0) %></strong> early access<% if @course.regular_price %>, then <%= number_to_currency(@course.regular_price, precision: 0) %><% end %></dd>
      <% end %>
      <dt>format</dt>
      <dd><%= @course.lessons.size %> written lessons, each with code you run</dd>
      <dt>code</dt>
      <dd><%= @course.lessons.map { |lesson| lesson["code"] }.uniq.join(" and ") %></dd>
    </dl>
    <% if @course.on_sale? %>
      <%= link_to "Buy for #{number_to_currency(@course.price, precision: 0)}", go_path("course", "#{@course.slug}/buy"), class: "button course-buy" %>
    <% else %>
      <p class="note course-soon"><strong>Launching soon.</strong> <%= mail_to Profile.email, "Email me", subject: "#{@course.title}: tell me when it launches" %> and I'll send you the link when it's out.</p>
    <% end %>
    <p class="rail-title">Start free</p>
    <ul>
      <% if @course.starter_url %><li><%= link_to "The free starter harness", go_path("course", "#{@course.slug}/starter") %></li><% end %>
      <% if sample %><li><%= link_to "Read lesson 1 free", blog_post_path(sample.slug) %></li><% end %>
    </ul>
  </aside>

  <h2>What it teaches</h2>
  <ol class="lessons">
    <% @course.lessons.each do |lesson| %>
      <li><strong><%= lesson["title"] %>.</strong> <%= lesson["line"] %> <span class="meta"><%= lesson["code"] %></span></li>
    <% end %>
  </ol>

  <h2>Who it's for</h2>
  <p>Engineers who have shipped an LLM feature, or are about to, and want to know whether a change made it better or worse. You should be comfortable reading TypeScript (five modules) and Ruby for the Rails module. It doesn't cover training models.</p>
  <p>It picks up where the free <%= link_to "LLM eval starter", work_item_path("llm-eval-starter") %> stops. The starter is a golden set, graders and a CI gate for a support-ticket triage feature. The course takes that same feature into production.</p>

  <h2>What's included</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Six written lessons. Each one has the problem, the mental model, a worked example with real output, common mistakes, an exercise and a checklist.</li>
    <li>Runnable code for every lesson, with tests. Five modules are TypeScript and one is a small Rails 8 app.</li>
    <li>Synthetic data, labeled as synthetic, and a mock model, so every module runs offline on your machine without an API key. Modules 2, 4 and 5 can also call Anthropic or OpenAI with your own key. The Anthropic paths have each been run once, and the numbers are in the course's proof file; the OpenAI paths haven't.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Want it done for you?</h2>
  <p>The <%= link_to "eval setup sprint", hire_path(anchor: "eval-sprint") %> on my hire page is this course applied to your feature: one week, a golden set from your real traffic, the harness in your repo, and a CI gate. The course is for doing it yourself.</p>

  <h2>Try it first</h2>
  <p>
    <% if @course.starter_url %>The <%= link_to "starter harness", go_path("course", "#{@course.slug}/starter") %> is free and open source.<% end %>
    <% if sample %>
      Lesson 1, <%= link_to sample.title, blog_post_path(sample.slug) %>, is free to read.
    <% end %>
    Questions? <%= mail_to Profile.email, "Email me" %>.
  </p>
</div>
